# Next.js app file organization

## Inside the App Router (`src/app/`)

Colocate route-specific code with underscore-prefixed folders so Next.js does not treat them as routes:

| Folder        | Use for |
|---------------|---------|
| `_components` | Components used only by this segment or its children |
| `_hooks`      | Hooks used only by this segment or its children |
| `_state`      | State modules (stores, context providers scoped to this subtree, etc.) |
| `_lib`        | Non-UI helpers shared by multiple features under this segment (formatters, mappers) — see [`lift-shared-route-utils.mdc`](lift-shared-route-utils.mdc) |

**Placement rule:** Put `_components`, `_hooks`, and `_state` at the **lowest common path** in the route tree that needs them.

- Used only by `src/app/dashboard/page.tsx` → `src/app/dashboard/_components/…`
- Shared by `dashboard/analytics` and `dashboard/reports` → `src/app/dashboard/_components/…`
- Shared by unrelated top-level areas → lift to `src/components/` (see below) or split duplicate-free boundaries deliberately

```text
src/app/
  layout.tsx
  page.tsx
  dashboard/
    _components/     ← dashboard-only UI
    _hooks/
    _state/
    page.tsx
    settings/
      _components/   ← settings subtree only
      page.tsx
```

In a monorepo this tree typically lives under `apps/web/src/app/`.

## App-wide code (`src/components/`)

Put **cross-cutting** components next to `app/`, not inside a single route:

`src/components/` — shell, nav, auth wrappers, and anything reused across many unrelated routes.

Do **not** put shadcn-style primitives or shared design-system widgets here.

## UI package (`packages/ui`)

**shadcn / design-system primitives** (Button, Card, Sonner, `cn`, global tokens) live in a **shared UI package** (commonly `packages/ui`). Import from the UI package in app code; keep `src/components/` for app composition, not reusable atoms.

If the project is not a monorepo, keep primitives in the project’s design-system folder instead — still separate from route-colocated `_components/`.

## Quick decision

1. Is it a shadcn-style primitive or token? → UI package / design-system folder
2. Is it used across the whole app with no natural route “owner”? → `src/components/`
3. Otherwise → `src/app/.../<segment>/_components|_hooks|_state/` at the lowest shared segment
